# Root .gitignore for the Zharp monorepo.
#
#   windows/   C# WinUI 3 app, built with MSBuild and the .NET SDK
#   macos/     Swift AppKit app, built with Swift Package Manager
#   linux/     placeholder, no code yet
#   shared/    platform neutral assets
#
# How to read the rules below: a pattern with no slash in it (like `bin/`) matches at
# any depth anywhere in the repo. A pattern that contains a slash (like
# `windows/installer/Output/`) is anchored to the directory holding this file, which is
# the repo root. That is why the two anchored rules carry a platform prefix here even
# though they did not in the per platform files they came from.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross platform: OS and editor droppings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Finder metadata. Turns up in any directory a macOS machine has browsed, so it is
# not scoped to macos/.
.DS_Store

# Machine local dev server config for the Claude Code preview pane. Personal to
# whoever is running it, never shared.
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# windows/  C# WinUI 3 app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# MSBuild and .NET build output. Left unanchored on purpose: every project under
# windows/src, windows/tests and windows/tools generates its own pair of these.
bin/
obj/

# Visual Studio per user settings (window layout, startup project, breakpoints).
*.user

# Visual Studio solution cache directory.
.vs/

# MSBuild binary logs, produced by `dotnet build -bl` when diagnosing a slow or
# failing build. Useful locally, far too large to commit.
*.binlog

# Inno Setup compiler output, the installer exe and its SHA-256 file. These are
# release artifacts, they get attached to the GitHub release instead.
windows/installer/Output/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macos/  Swift AppKit app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Swift Package Manager build directory and its per user state.
.build/
.swiftpm/

# Assembled Zharp.app and the packaged dmg. Release artifacts, same reasoning as
# the Windows installer output above.
dist/

# Xcode projects and workspaces are generated on demand from Package.swift
# (`swift package generate-xcodeproj`, or just opening Package.swift in Xcode).
# Nothing here is a source of truth, so nothing here is committed.
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace

# Generated from macos/Assets/logos by macos/Scripts/make-icon.sh, and rebuilt by
# `make icon` as part of `make app`.
macos/Packaging/AppIcon.icns

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# linux/  nothing to ignore yet
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no Linux code and no toolkit chosen, so there is no build output to
# ignore. Add the rules here when that changes. See linux/README.md.
